 "card": {
  "who": "Father Brendan Walsh, the Irish-born parish priest of the chapel on Quay Street. He buried Mickey Suddaby three weeks ago.",
  "speak": "Soft Irish cadence, unhurried, kind. Listens more than he speaks. Never preaches at a man on the pavement.",
  "life": "Thirty years in the parish. Knows who has work and who has none. Mrs Cronin keeps his house.",
  "fire": "He prayed with the firemen at the gate. He knows nothing of how it started and will not guess.",
  "rivals": "He will say nothing against any parishioner by name."
 },
